{{<shell}}{{$content}}
<p class="crumb"><a href="{{backUrl}}">&larr; Invites</a></p>
<h1>{{heading}}</h1>

<form class="editor" method="post" action="{{backUrl}}">
  <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{csrf}}">
  <input type="hidden" name="action" value="create">
  <div class="field"><label for="i-email">their email address</label>
    <input id="i-email" type="email" name="email" placeholder="someone@example.com" required autofocus></div>
  <div class="doing">
    <button class="btn" type="submit">Send the invitation</button>
  </div>
  <p class="hint">That is the whole form, and pressing it sends. There is one invitation for the
    whole community, written once, so nobody has to compose a sentence under pressure and every
    invitation reads the same.</p>
</form>

<h2>What they will get</h2>
<div class="preview">
  <div class="from">{{community}}</div>
  {{#previewSubject}}<div class="tagline">{{previewSubject}}</div>{{/previewSubject}}
  <p class="lead">{{previewLead}}</p>
  {{#previewAbout}}<p>{{previewAbout}}</p>{{/previewAbout}}
  <p><span class="fakebtn">{{previewButton}}</span></p>
  <p class="dim">Using {{community}} means you accept its terms and privacy policy.</p>
</div>
<div class="doing"><a class="btn quiet" href="{{wordingUrl}}">Edit this wording</a></div>
<p class="hint">This is the community's invitation, not this one &mdash; one message for everybody,
  written once. The words live with every other message this server sends
  {{#overridden}}and this community has written its own{{/overridden}}{{^overridden}}and this is the
  wording that ships, which keeps improving with the software until somebody changes it{{/overridden}}.
  The shape around them &mdash; the button, the plain-text half, the footer &mdash; stays in the
  software.</p>

<h2>The sequence</h2>
<p class="hint">{{cadence}} Each one is the same invitation with the same link &mdash; not three
  invitations &mdash; so an open or a sign-up counts once however many messages it took. The third
  says it is the last one, and it is.</p>

{{#canBulk}}
<h2>A lot of people at once</h2>
<form class="editor" method="post" action="{{backUrl}}">
  <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{csrf}}">
  <input type="hidden" name="action" value="bulk">
  <div><label for="i-bulk">addresses</label>
    <textarea id="i-bulk" name="addresses" rows="7" placeholder="one per line, or commas, or pasted straight out of a mail client"></textarea>
    <p class="hint">Commas, semicolons, newlines and <span class="mono">Name &lt;addr@example.org&gt;</span>
      all work. Duplicates are dropped. At most {{bulkMax}} at a time &mdash; past that it is a
      mailing list rather than an invitation, and every spam filter will treat it as one.</p></div>
  <div class="doing">
    <button class="btn" type="submit">Invite them all</button>
    <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="send" checked> send them now</label>
  </div>
</form>
{{/canBulk}}
{{/content}}{{/shell}}
